{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7753","id":5212930372,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNrcBRA","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7753","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7753.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7753.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7753","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7753/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7753/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7753/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/01d3aee3f586b29b71eb1801bcd08d9f2fdbc02e","number":7753,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(aggregator): bound /api/board.json to the board the page shows (#5082)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\n`/api/board.json` — the machine twin of `/board` — now returns **the board the page shows**, not the whole completion log.\n\n## Why (root cause, named)\n\nThe endpoint built its payload from `boardContext()` with no done policy and no strip limit:\n\n- **1 720 cards**, of which 1 483 were `done` (the full 7-day window) while `renderBoardBody` renders at most `DONE_STRIP_RENDER_LIMIT` (100) newest done cards.\n- **2 903 linked items** — the closure of every ref *every* card had ever linked. 2 546 of those items were reachable only through done cards, and only 337 cards were actually rendered.\n- Total: **2 717 429 B** measured on the live laptop aggregator (`127.0.0.1:4870`).\n\nThat payload is past the aggregator's own **2 MB `MAX_CACHED_RESPONSE_BYTES`** (`src/assembly-deadline.ts`), so the 503/timeout path could never serve it as a stale response — and every request re-read the entire item closure, which is the shared assembly the steward's `000`/empty-reply observations trace to.\n\n## Change\n\n- New `src/board-json.ts` (`boardJsonBody`): applies `applyBoardDonePolicy` (7-day done age-out + retired ROADMAP Done-table class) and the shared done-strip limit, then ships **only the items the visible cards link to**. Each card already carries its own `links`, so `items` is a resolution lookup, not a dump.\n- New `selectVisibleDoneCards` in `board-policy.ts`: the newest-N done selection, shared by `renderBoardBody` and the JSON twin so the two can never disagree again.\n- `/api/board.json` view branch filters the **already-bounded** board and keeps only those cards' items (no reintroduction of the closure).\n- Compact JSON for this endpoint (`jsonCompact`) — no 2-space padding for a machine consumer.\n- `?done=all` restores the full done strip, mirroring `/board?done=all`.\n\nMeasured shape: **2 717 429 B → ~439 KB** on the same data (83.4% smaller, comfortably under the 2 MB cache limit).\n\n## Tests\n\n- New `test/board-json-5082.test.ts` (6 cases): live-only items, 7-day age-out, retired Done-table class, newest-first strip cap, `?done=all`, custom limit, and bounded output under a 2 400-card completion log (>10× smaller than the unbounded form).\n- `test/boot.test.ts`: every shipped item resolves a link a shipped card carries; response is not pretty-printed.\n- `bun test` (targeted aggregates): **73 pass**. `bunx tsc --noEmit`: no `src/` errors (the two `test/` errors are pre-existing on `origin/main`).\n\n## Notes / not in scope\n\n- This bounds the payload and the per-request item closure; it does not re-architect the facet assembly (explicitly out of scope in the packet). The `/program` HTML size concern is a separate symptom already split out under #5082's history.\n\nFixes #5082\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796746620&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7753&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7753&signature=81133da28c170c24a2ec5bd1d2ad5706d20f7c63a4ff34f368bf3a353fce67bf\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7753?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T16:16:56Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T19:39:29Z","closed_at":"2026